Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: recognize YU08 dual-channel temperature sensors

Use the existing Bus/Address and Name/Name1 configuration contract.
YU08 clients are instantiated by the board device tree.
Both temperature channels report unsigned byte Celsius values.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform specific]

diff --git a/src/HwmonTempMain.cpp b/src/HwmonTempMain.cpp
--- a/src/HwmonTempMain.cpp
+++ b/src/HwmonTempMain.cpp
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@ static const I2CDeviceTypeMap sensorTypes{
     {"W83773G", I2CDeviceType{"w83773g", true}},
     {"TMP451", I2CDeviceType{"tmp451", true}},
     {"CT7451", I2CDeviceType{"ct7451", true}},
+    {"YU08", I2CDeviceType{"yu08", true}},
 };

 static struct SensorParams
@@ -426,6 +427,12 @@ void createSensors(

             const SensorData& sensorData = findSensorCfg->second.sensorData;
             const std::string& sensorType = findSensorCfg->second.interface;
+            if (sensorType == "xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.YU08")
+            {
+                thisSensorParameters.minValue = 0;
+                thisSensorParameters.maxValue = 255;
+            }
+
             const SensorBaseConfigMap& baseConfigMap =
                 findSensorCfg->second.config;
             std::vector<std::string>& hwmonName = findSensorCfg->second.name;
